Subject: [overlay 0016] Stereoscopic view offset for visionOS 3D

Add cl_stereo_offset + V_SetStereoOffset(): shift the view origin sideways along
cl.v_right (parallel cameras, no vertical parallax) just before R_RenderFrame. The
immersive shell renders the frame once per eye with +/- half the eye separation to
produce true stereo depth. 0 = mono (no effect on the iOS/2D builds).
Apply: patch -p1 -d vendor/q2repro < this

diff --git a/src/client/view.c b/src/client/view.c
index 5d088ad8..dadde4d5 100644
--- a/src/client/view.c
+++ b/src/client/view.c
@@ -528,6 +528,12 @@ void V_FogParamsChanged(unsigned bits, unsigned color_bits, unsigned hf_start_co
         cur->height.end.dist = params->height.end.dist;
 }
 
+// [stereo overlay] Horizontal eye offset (world units along the view's right vector) applied to
+// the view origin just before the scene is rendered; 0 = mono. The visionOS 3D shell renders the
+// frame once per eye with +/- half the eye separation to produce true stereoscopic depth.
+float cl_stereo_offset;
+void V_SetStereoOffset(float offset) { cl_stereo_offset = offset; }
+
 /*
 ==================
 V_RenderView
@@ -566,6 +572,11 @@ void V_RenderView(void)
         cl.refdef.vieworg[1] += 1.0f / 16;
         cl.refdef.vieworg[2] += 1.0f / 16;
 
+        // [stereo overlay] shift the eye sideways for stereoscopic 3D (parallel cameras — same
+        // view angles, so no vertical parallax). cl.v_right is set by CL_AddEntities above.
+        if (cl_stereo_offset)
+            VectorMA(cl.refdef.vieworg, cl_stereo_offset, cl.v_right, cl.refdef.vieworg);
+
         cl.refdef.x = scr.vrect.x;
         cl.refdef.y = scr.vrect.y;
         cl.refdef.width = scr.vrect.width;
